               "headline":  "Strong Q3, but AI sell-off and Trump tax threat break the 200-day line",
               "summary":  "Equinix fell 4.89% to $968.22 on 20 Nov 2026 on about 1.8x normal volume and closed below its EMA 200. The trigger was not company news. AI-infrastructure stocks sold off broadly, and on the same day President Trump threatened a \"tremendous tax\" on US firms that build AI data centres abroad. The business itself looks solid. Q3 results on 28 Oct showed revenue up 11% to $2.571B and record gross bookings of $533M (+35%), and 2026 guidance went up for a third time. The short-term chart is weak; the long-term thesis is unchanged.",
