               "opportunityCheck":  "The scores look broadly right. Exposure at 9 fits: Equinix gives no AI share of bookings, and neoclouds are under 2% of monthly recurring revenue. Position at 17 is earned by the interconnection ecosystem, which added 6,900 net cross-connects in Q3. I would raise bottleneck \u0026 pricing power by about one point, because new-deal pricing rose 12% and management plans to reprice renewals while power stays scarce. Optionality could rise once Inference Exchange and Fabric One reach general availability in 2027 with disclosed pricing, but neither is proven yet.",
               "technical":  "Trend: the 20 Nov close of $968.22 is below all three exponential moving averages (EMAs, smoothed average prices): EMA 50 at $1,023.54, EMA 100 at $1,024.50 and EMA 200 at $1,001.79. The 50 and 100 are flat and almost on top of each other, both still above the 200. That points to a stalled medium-term uptrend rather than a clear reversal, but losing the 200-day line is a warning. Momentum: MACD (the gap between a fast and a slow average) is 1.8, below its signal line at 6.62, with a histogram of -4.82. That is a bearish crossover. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) is 39.11, so momentum is weak but not oversold. Volatility: the price sits on the lower Bollinger Band at $965.44 (a band 2 standard deviations around the 20-day mean of $1,024.85), which means it is stretched to the downside in the short term. It is about 14% below the 52-week high of $1,128.68 and 34% above the 52-week low of $720.62. Volume of 1.33M shares was about 1.8x the 20-day average of 753K, which confirms real selling. Support is near the lower band at about $965; resistance is the EMA cluster at $1,000–1,025.",
               "fundamental":  "Equinix rents space, power and, above all, connections. Customers pay to cross-connect with clouds, networks and partners inside its 270+ sites, which makes the ecosystem sticky. In Q3 2026 (reported 28 Oct), revenue was $2.571B (+11%) and adjusted EBITDA $1.321B (+15%). AFFO per share was $11.64, up 12% excluding a one-off atNorth fee. Net interconnections grew by 6,900, and Fabric revenue rose 24%. Full-year guidance now implies about 12% revenue growth and an EBITDA margin of about 51%; Q4 revenue is guided at $2.684–2.724B. AI shows up mainly through inference and hybrid enterprise AI. New customers average 7 kW per cabinet versus 5 kW for those leaving, liquid-cooling bookings rose more than 10x, and 15% of 2027 retail capacity is already pre-sold. Capex of $5–6B funds a 3 GW pipeline.",
