               "caution":  "The chart turned weak on 20 Nov: the price is below all three EMAs, MACD has crossed down, and the selling came on heavy volume. The trigger was macro and political, and that kind of pressure can last even when results are good. The overseas data-centre tax remark is vague, but it matters for a US company with a large share of its sites abroad. A concrete proposal would be a real risk. Equinix also spends heavily ($5–6B of capex in 2026) and, as a REIT, is sensitive to interest rates. Tighter funding or higher bond yields would weigh on the stock.",
               "opportunity":  "Nothing in the 20 Nov drop came from Equinix itself. Its latest numbers (28 Oct) were strong: record bookings, 12% higher pricing on new deals and a third guidance raise. If the sell-off is mostly sentiment, the gap between the price and the business has widened. The stock sits at the lower Bollinger Band with RSI near 39, and published analyst targets are well above the current price. Inference Exchange and Fabric One add new AI-linked products in 2027. Long-term holders will want to see whether Q4 bookings, 60% of target already done by late October, hold up.",
